# MindStone for Claude Code — user-specific orchestrator content
# Each developer's Cairn-like instance is private to them; the repo ships
# the framework (hooks, schema, templates, design docs) but NOT individual
# identity, user profile, session log, or accumulated personal memory.
# See orchestrator/memory/CAIRN_DESIGN_v0.3.md §8 (public/private boundary).
orchestrator/IDENTITY.md
orchestrator/USER.md
orchestrator/LOG.md
orchestrator/DOCS_UPDATED.md
# The memory directory is ignored WHOLESALE, with an explicit allowlist.
#
# It used to be a denylist of filename prefixes (feedback_*, project_*, reference_*,
# lineage_*, MEMORY.md). That fails OPEN: any memory whose name did not match a
# listed prefix was tracked by default. `design_synapse.md` matched none of them and
# sat tracked in a public repo for months, and every future naming convention would
# have done the same -- silently, because a file that is simply never ignored looks
# identical to a file someone decided to publish.
#
# Ignore everything, allow back the few framework files by name. A new memory is
# private by default; publishing one becomes a deliberate act that shows up in review.
#
# The INDEX is private for the same reason the memories are: every line summarises a
# gitignored file -- names, hosts, projects, people. It ships as
# onboarding/MEMORY.md.example instead, like IDENTITY/USER/AGENTS.
#
# Enforced by orchestrator/runbooks/privacy_scan.py and .github/workflows/privacy-scan.yml.
orchestrator/memory/*
!orchestrator/memory/.gitkeep
!orchestrator/memory/README.md
# User-private skills (project-specific scripts referencing private infra,
# IPs, credentials, keys). Substrate-mechanic skills can be opted in by
# moving them out of skills/ into hooks/ or by carving a sub-path exception.
orchestrator/skills/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# KEPT (framework-level, team/public-shareable):
#   orchestrator/memory/CAIRN_DESIGN_*.md   — design documentation
#   orchestrator/memory/.migrate_frontmatter.py — schema migration utility

# Wake-daemon config (per-machine; secret_file path is sensitive)
orchestrator/config/wake-daemon.toml
